		<title type="html"><![CDATA[NaturalMotion is hiring physics developers (SF &amp; Oxford)]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=2980#p2980"><![CDATA[
<a href="http://www.naturalmotion.com" class="postlink">http://www.naturalmotion.com</a><br><br>NaturalMotion is looking to further expand its behavior authoring / game physics team responsible for the creation of cutting edge AI behaviors for interactive 3D character control.<br><br>We are recruiting candidates for this position who:<br><br>- Are comfortable with advanced engineering maths<br>- Have a familiarity with 3D animation tools<br>- Have a good eye for believable human motions<br>- Worked with articulated bodies and/or physical animation<br>- Experience with third party physics engines: (Havok, PhysX, ODE, Newton, Bullet, etc) or in-house / proprietary physics engines<br><br>We welcome candidates from an engineering or applied mathematical background with innovative ideas for synthesizing physical human behavior, as well as animators and TDs with a strong technical capability.<br><br>Successful applicants will be responsible for designing and implementing dynamically simulated characters and their real time controllers.<br><br>Location: San Francisco or Oxford (UK)<br><br>Mail resume/cover letter to:<br><a href="mailto:careers@naturalmotion.com">careers@naturalmotion.com</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=418">jobs</a> — Sat Dec 23, 2006 7:00 pm</p><hr />
